  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(t)=4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+5t+11$ be the number of machines infected by the computer virus after $t$ days. To find the average rate of growth of $f(t)$ over the first week, we use the average rate of change formula on the interval $[0,7]$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δt} & =\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(7)-f(0)}{7-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{[4(7)^{3}-2(7)^{2}+5(7)+11]-[4(0)^{3}-2(0)^{2}+5(0)+11]}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1309}{7} \\\\  & =187\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average rate of growth over the first week is $187$ machines per day.",
